          "aggregates": [
            {
              "id": "shop.cart.basket",
              "slug": "basket",
              "name": "Basket",
              "readme": "# Basket\n\nThe one mutable thing between a customer arriving and an order existing: a\nvisitor's or a customer's lines, under one lock. It changes as items go in and\nout and stops changing the moment it is checked out; from then on the order is\nsomebody else's aggregate and the basket is a record of what was bought.\n\n## States\n\n`open` → `checked-out` | `abandoned` | `merged`, and nothing leads back. The\ntable is `status.ts`, and `moveTo` is the only way through it; lines go in\nand out only while the basket is `open`. Each way out publishes: checkout\n`BasketCheckedOut`, the sweep `BasketAbandoned`, a merge `BasketMerged` from\nthe basket that emptied.\n\n## Invariants\n\n- One currency, set by the first line and never changed (cart.0002).\n- A line's price is what it was given when added, never recomputed (cart.0003).\n- One to 99 of a SKU per line; at most 50 distinct SKUs.\n- A version travels with every write; a write from a stale read is refused.",
              "root": "Basket",
              "entities": [],
              "valueObjects": [],
              "operations": [],
              "events": [
                {
                  "id": "shop.cart.basket.BasketCheckedOut",
                  "slug": "basket-checked-out",
                  "name": "BasketCheckedOut",
                  "versions": [
                    {
                      "version": "v1",
                      "doc": "The basket is frozen. This is the handoff: whoever places the order listens\nfor it, and pricing expires the quote it issued.",
                      "source": "examples/shop/cart/src/domain/basket/events/basket-checked-out.ts",
                      "fields": [
                        {
                          "name": "basketId",
                          "type": "string",
                          "doc": ""
                        },
                        {
                          "name": "customerId",
                          "type": "string",
                          "doc": ""
                        },
                        {
                          "name": "items",
